{"base_rate":0.2864651773981603,"brier":0.11374375821287779,"bss":0.44353152719347144,"bss_hi":0.5560615562226887,"bss_lo":0.2766357826108414,"chart":{"base":[433.4,52.6],"fp":[170.8,265.9],"lead":"62,254.2 272,228.7 482,208.7 692,159","note":{"base":"skill 0.44 — higher than 84% of cities","fp":"low end -3pp, high end +24pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 54% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 0%; promised 91% → rained 67%"},"rel":"68.1,466 218.6,439.3 635.2,175.2"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1395532194480946,"ess":410.76704545454345,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Hiroshima</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Hiroshima rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 1.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.44, ranked 35 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(10&ndash;114) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>221</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>31%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>231</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Hiroshima</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.44</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>10&ndash;114\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Hiroshima &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Hiroshima\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.06407239819004,380.3529411764706 72.16,345.07246376811594 105.6253488372093,305.8139534883721 191.68157894736842,204.78947368421052 306.7530769230769,88.0 404.82805194805195,19.575757575757564 404.82805194805195,32.18181818181819 306.7530769230769,162.66666666666669 191.68157894736842,281.42105263157896 105.6253488372093,356.6046511627907 72.16,382.0 58.06407239819004,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"277.72667542706967\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"277.72667542706967\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.06407239819004,382.0 72.16,382.0 105.6253488372093,369.30232558139534 191.68157894736842,348.4736842105263 306.7530769230769,270.0 404.82805194805195,92.06060606060606\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 221 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.06407239819004\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"72.16\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 13%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"105.6253488372093\" cy=\"369.30232558139534\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 38%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"191.68157894736842\" cy=\"348.4736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 70%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"306.7530769230769\" cy=\"270.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 231 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"404.82805194805195\" cy=\"92.06060606060606\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(29%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Hiroshima the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.73) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.07).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'>0.066</td><td class='num'>16.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.285</td><td class='num'>21.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'>0.392</td><td class='num'>14.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.728</td><td class='num'>5.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":34.4,"lon":132.45,"n":761,"n_cities":213,"name":"Hiroshima","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00018099547511312217,"n":221,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.04,"n":69,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.13453488372093023,"n":86,"obs":0.03488372093023256,"sig":true},{"hi":0.55,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.37763157894736843,"n":76,"obs":0.09210526315789473,"s